-- title:
--   Places above v in an algebraically closed constant extension
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a perfect field, $K$ an algebraically closed field, and $F_0$, $F$ fields, with $k$-algebra structures on $K$, $F_0$ and $F$, a $K$-algebra structure on $F$ and an $F_0$-algebra structure on $F$, compatible in the sense that $k \to K \to F$ and $k \to F_0 \to F$ both agree with $k \to F$. Assume [`AlgebraicCurve.IsCurveOver k F₀`](def/AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver.html#L15) and [`AlgebraicCurve.IsCurveOver K F`](def/AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver.html#L15), i.e. each of $F_0/k$ and $F/K$ has the property that every nonzero element has a divisor of degree $0$ recording its orders at all places, that every place has residue field finite over the base field, and that the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank $1$ over the function field. Assume further that $F_0$ is generated over $k$ by a finite subset; that the $K$-subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $F_0$ is all of $F$; and that the image of $F_0$ is linearly disjoint from $K$ over $k$, in the form: for every $n$, every $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to F_0$ that is $k$-linearly independent and every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to K$ with $\sum_i c_i f_i = 0$ in $F$, all $c_i$ vanish. Here a place of $F/K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$, whose underlying ring is a principal ideal ring, and the degree of a place $v$ of $F_0/k$ is $\deg v = [\kappa(v):k]$, the $k$-rank of the residue field of its valuation ring. Then, for a place $v$ of $F_0/k$ with valuation ring $\mathcal O_v$: the set of places $W$ of $F/K$ with $\mathcal O_W \cap F_0 = \mathcal O_v$ (pullback of $\mathcal O_W$ along $F_0 \to F$) is finite; its cardinality equals $\deg v$; and any two such places $W_1, W_2$ coincide as soon as, for all $f \in \mathcal O_v$ and all $a \in K$, the element $f - a$ of $F$ being a non-unit of $\mathcal O_{W_1}$ implies it is a non-unit of $\mathcal O_{W_2}$.
--
--   This is the classical description of the fibre of the constant-field extension $F_0K/K$ over a place $v$ of $F_0/k$ when the new constant field $K$ is algebraically closed: there are exactly $\deg v$ places above $v$, matching the $k$-embeddings $\kappa(v) \hookrightarrow K$, and such a place is pinned down by the residue values it assigns to elements of $\mathcal O_v$. It is used in the descent arguments for divisors and places over a constant extension, and in the count of fixed points of iterated Frobenius-type maps on places.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_natCard_setOf_comap_eq_eq_deg_of_linearDisjoint.lean

